_at":"2020-09-20T18:00:03Z","closed_at":"2020-09-20T18:00:02Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nWhen creating a temporary table I can't detect it when I run .has_table() as it returns  `False`. I can see some work has been done on detecting temp tables in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/5506 but it doesn't look like this is covered.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nThat `.has_table()` returns `True`\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\n```py\r\nconn = engine.connect()\r\nstmt= \"\"\"\r\nCREATE TABLE #my_table\r\n(\r\n    col1 VARCHAR(50),\r\n    col2 int\r\n)\r\n\"\"\"\r\nconn.execute(sql)\r\nconn.dialect.has_table(conn,\"#my_table\")\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: Windows\r\n - Python: 3.8.2\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 1.3.17\r\n - Database: SQL Server 14\r\n - DBAPI: PyODBC\r\n - Driver: ODBC Driver 17 for SQL Server\r\n\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://